	<description>Peter Carey's Booker Prize winning novel imagines Australia's youth, before its dynamic passions became dangerous habits. It is also a startling and unusual love story. &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Oscar is a young English clergyman who has broken with his past and developed a disturbing talent for gambling. A country girl of singular ambition, Lucinda moves to Sydney, driven by dreams of self-reliance and the building of an industrial Utopia. Together this unlikely pair create and are created by the spectacle of mid-nineteenth century Australia. &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Peter Carey's visionary brilliance, and his capacity to delight and surprise, propel this story to its stunning conclusion.</description>
